The probe file is removed. Good.

Also topology: v0.4.0 tag contains a merge "Merge pull request #99 from re-cinq/lore/implementation-loop/issue-95" (c610755) whose ancestry includes 684b294 (current HEAD/base) and the fix 9114ffa. So in the tag timeline the ticket got resolved in PR #99 AFTER the current base. The clone's origin/main is pinned at the pre-fix point. So the ticket is genuinely open at this branch's base — I write red tests. This matches the loop-bench design: tags hold future history; the working branch is at the pre-fix point.

